            <ArticleTitle>[Painful bullous keratopathy treatment using anterior stromal puncture combined with amniotic membrane transplantation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of painful bullous keratopathy (PBK) treated using author's procedure of anterior stromal puncture (ASP) combined with amniotic membrane transplantation (AMT) is presented. ASP combined with AMT can be effective option for pain relief and promotion of epithelial healing in patients with PBK and poor visual potential.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
